-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Oct  4 06:35:44 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.2.37:
  * Eager backend: quantize_signed_int4_rowwise is now a thin wrapper
    over a new _quantize_signed_int4_rowwise_unpacked, which returns
    signed INT4 codes in INT8 storage without packing nibbles. The
    public function keeps its name, signature and packed return value
  * Ascend convrot_w4a4_linear keeps the activation's INT4 codes in
    INT8 containers instead of packing them and immediately unpacking
    them again, cutting a pack/unpack round-trip off the NPU path.
    Ascend RoPE coverage is now documented as requiring
    npu_rotary_mul with rotary_mode (RMS-RoPE also npu_rms_norm)
  * CUDA W4A8 GEMM now sizes its weight chunks from the device L2
    cache: below 16 MiB of L2 a chunk cannot stay resident, so the
    decode runs full-width instead. Upstream measures up to 20%
    faster at M=512 on a 3080
  * Remainder of the release is CUDA and HIP kernel work (dlpack
    bindings, CUTLASS int8 GEMM, W4A8 requant, int8 attention), not
    compiled in this CPU-only build

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Sep 29 08:27:17 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.2.36:
  * New Huawei Ascend NPU backend. It registers only when torch-npu
    and an Ascend device are present, so list_backends() reports it
    unavailable on this build and the import is a no-op without
    torch-npu
  * Eager backend: fp16_conv3d and group_norm_silu_pad3d accept an
    out= destination, and the new fp16_conv3d_out and
    group_norm_silu_pad3d_out ops write straight into an
    NDHWC-ordered output or view, so a tiled conv needs no per-tile
    copies
  * group_norm_silu_pad3d gains zero_pad= for models whose
    convolutions zero-pad the spatial border instead of
    reflecting it
  * W6A8 grouped weight quantization next to W4A8, in the same
    packed row layout with the bit depth implied by the row width
  * The is_available() probes (sol_attn, flash decode, INT8
    attention, fused DeltaNet) now take a torch.device rather than
    an int index and report False for a non-CUDA device; a caller
    passing an integer index breaks
  * Fused DeltaNet decode now declines below SM75, which the shared
    memory check alone used to wave through on Volta
  * Remainder of the release is CUDA and HIP kernel work (int8
    attention, W4A8 GEMM, 256-wide flash decode), not compiled in
    this CPU-only build

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Sep 22 18:09:05 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.2.35:
  * New gated-delta (DeltaNet) decode ops in the package
    namespace: gated_delta_decode_fused, deltanet_conv_step and
    a gated_delta_decode_is_available probe. The kernels behind
    them are CUDA and HIP only, so the probe reports False on
    this build
  * Remainder of the release is CUDA and HIP kernel work, which
    this build does not compile: it ships the pure-Python eager
    backend only

